// =====================================================================
// CHANNEL TAG + SIS RECONCILIATION
//
// STATUS: investigation OPEN, not resolved. An earlier version of this file
// assumed Rs 236 L was the correct Primary SIS FY26 figure and that a Rs 250 L
// reading was an offtake-derivation artifact. That is RULED OUT: File 2's own
// explicit Channel field (the intended source of truth) independently nets to
// Rs 250.17 L for SIS FY26 -- confirmed by summing Inv. Net value(LOC) filtered
// on Channel="SIS" directly from the raw source, with no offtake data involved.
// Checked and ruled out as drivers of the Rs 14.16 L gap: negative/return lines
// (-Rs 30.24 L, already netted in), MRN returns and cancelled invoices (netting
// to the same Rs 250.17 L), and duplicate invoice lines (<Rs 0.5 L impact). See
// docs/SIS_Reconciliation.md for the full investigation and what's needed to
// close it (the source/definition of the Rs 236 L reference figure).
//
// What these measures still do:
//  - Primary (File 2 / Fact Primary Article) has an EXPLICIT Channel column
//    (MT / EB2B / SIS) -> treated as the source of truth for Primary SIS.
//  - Offtake (store x article) has NO Channel -> derived below via a calc
//    column: Store Code override -> Chain default -> "Unmapped" (never dropped).
//  - Primary vs Offtake SIS is reconciled and any gap is located by chain --
//    useful for tagging offtake by channel, but NOT what explains the Rs 14.16 L
//    Primary-side gap (that gap exists entirely within File 2 itself).
// =====================================================================

// ---------- Calculated COLUMN on 'Fact Offtake Sales' ----------
// (Modeling > New column, on the Fact Offtake Sales table)
Offtake Channel =
VAR _byStore =
    LOOKUPVALUE ( 'Channel Map Store'[Channel],
        'Channel Map Store'[Store Code], 'Fact Offtake Sales'[Store Code] )
VAR _byChain =
    LOOKUPVALUE ( 'Channel Map Chain'[Channel],
        'Channel Map Chain'[Chain], 'Fact Offtake Sales'[Chain] )
RETURN COALESCE ( _byStore, _byChain, "Unmapped" )

// ---------- Channel splits ----------
// PRIMARY (authoritative — explicit Channel from File 2 / Fact Primary Article)
Primary NSV (Article) = SUM ( 'Fact Primary Article'[Primary NSV] )
Primary SIS  = CALCULATE ( [Primary NSV (Article)], 'Fact Primary Article'[Channel] = "SIS" )
Primary EB2B = CALCULATE ( [Primary NSV (Article)], 'Fact Primary Article'[Channel] = "EB2B" )
Primary MT   = CALCULATE ( [Primary NSV (Article)], 'Fact Primary Article'[Channel] = "MT" )

// OFFTAKE (derived Channel)
Offtake SIS  = CALCULATE ( [Total Offtake NSV], 'Fact Offtake Sales'[Offtake Channel] = "SIS" )
Offtake EB2B = CALCULATE ( [Total Offtake NSV], 'Fact Offtake Sales'[Offtake Channel] = "EB2B" )
Offtake MT   = CALCULATE ( [Total Offtake NSV], 'Fact Offtake Sales'[Offtake Channel] = "MT" )
Offtake Unmapped Channel = CALCULATE ( [Total Offtake NSV], 'Fact Offtake Sales'[Offtake Channel] = "Unmapped" )

// ---------- Display in Cr (Indian) ----------
Primary SIS (Cr) = DIVIDE ( [Primary SIS], 10000000 )
Offtake SIS (Cr) = DIVIDE ( [Offtake SIS], 10000000 )

// ---------- SIS reconciliation ----------
SIS Variance = [Primary SIS] - [Offtake SIS]
SIS Variance (Cr) = DIVIDE ( [SIS Variance], 10000000 )
SIS Variance (Lacs) = DIVIDE ( [SIS Variance], 100000 )
SIS Match =
IF ( ABS ( [SIS Variance] ) < 100000, "OK (< Rs 1 L)", "Gap - investigate" )

// Channel coverage: how much offtake resolved to a real channel (not Unmapped)
Offtake Channel Coverage % =
1 - DIVIDE ( [Offtake Unmapped Channel], [Total Offtake NSV] )

// Sanity note: Primary SIS must be sourced ONLY from File 2's explicit
// Channel = "SIS" ([Primary SIS] above) — never derived from the ship-to
// primary (File 1 is MT-only, no Channel). [Primary SIS] correctly nets to
// ~Rs 2.50 Cr FY26 per the raw source; that reading is NOT the bug (see the
// header note above) — the open question is what the Rs 2.36 Cr reference
// figure is actually defined as.

// ---------- Reconciliation table helper ----------
// Build a table visual: rows = Chain, values = [Primary SIS (Cr)],
// [Offtake SIS (Cr)], [SIS Variance (Lacs)]. Sort by SIS Variance to see the
// chains driving the ~Rs 14 L gap. Add 'Offtake Channel' = "Unmapped" as a
// slicer to list stores whose channel didn't resolve.
